    {
      "text": "ON THE COMPUTATION OF THE DIFFERENCE GALOIS GROUPS OF ORDER THREE EQUATIONS — In this paper we consider the problem of computing the diﬀere nce Galois groups of order three equations for a large\n\n**ON THE COMPUTATION OF THE DIFFERENCE GALOIS GROUPS OF ORDER THREE EQUATIONS**\n\n*THOMAS DREYFUS AND MARINA POULET*\n\n37 pp, 18 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this paper we consider the problem of computing the diﬀere nce Galois groups of order three equations for a large class of diﬀerenc e operators including the shift operator (Case S), the q-diﬀerence operator (Case Q), the Mahler operator (Case M) a nd the elliptic case (Case E). We show that the general problem c an be reduced to several ancillary problems. We prove criteria to detect the irreduc ible and imprimitive Galois groups. Finally, we give a suﬃcient condition of diﬀerentia l transcendence of solutions of order three diﬀerence equations. We also compute the diﬀe rence Galois group of an equation suggested by Wadim Zudilin.\n\n**Outline.** 1 Introduction; 2.1 Galois groups; Notations and conventions; 2 Difference algebra; 2.3 From theory to practice; 3 Galois groups of difference systems; 3.1 The reducible case; 3.2 The imprimitive case; 3.3 The primitive case; 4 Galois groups of equations of order one and ; 4.2 Galois groups of diagonal systems; 5 Galois groups of equations of order two; 6.1 Reducible case; 6 Galois groups of equations of order three; 6.2 Imprimitive case; 6.4 Summary; 7 Application to the differential transcendenc; References",
